# Media Ingestion And Normalization

- Accept common creator upload formats, but normalize them server-side before the app depends on them.
- Validate mime type, dimensions, size, and checksum before marking an asset as publishable.
- Keep the original file when needed, but serve processed variants by default.
- Track processing state explicitly so upload, processing, retry, and failure are visible in the UI.
- Do not let client code rely on temporary upload paths or raw unprocessed files.
- Keep image conversion, subtitle validation, and manifest validation in dedicated processing utilities or workers.
